    "tranche": "T6",
    "tranche_reason": "The study evaluates head-ablation methods on a synthetic copying task and arithmetic control, not IOI behavior or the IOI circuit. Its methodological discussion does not test whether the IOI circuit or any listed version holds.",
    "gate_note": "The paper cites the IOI-circuit study but does not use IOI prompts, identify or test its seven head classes, or measure IOI performance. The results below concern GPT-2-family head ablations on other tasks; they do not test V1–V6.",
    "test_reason": "The study runs no IOI prompts and studies no IOI heads or circuit metrics. It tests single-head zero-ablation methodology on a synthetic induction-style copying task and an arithmetic control in GPT-2 small and DistilGPT2. The IOI paper (ref [5]) appears only in a list of circuit work that validates claims against baselines. 'cites_only' fits better than 'discusses', since no argument about the IOI circuit or its evaluation is made.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Mostly correct. It should add that on DistilGPT2 the selected heads also exceeded the specificity control (p=0.001), and that the authors claim only an intervention effect, not a mechanistic role.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "The study audits post-projection versus pre-projection zero-ablation and evaluates synthetic copying and arithmetic tasks; it does not reproduce the IOI circuit-finding or IOI evaluation recipe.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Outcomes differ with hook placement (post- versus pre-projection), metric (exact-match accuracy versus log-probability), task (copying versus arithmetic), and model (GPT-2 small versus DistilGPT2). GPT-2 specificity also differs between the primary N = 200 run and the N = 500 rerun.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Naive post-projection head ablation is nearly uncorrelated with correct pre-projection ablation (r=0.057 in GPT-2; r=0.001 in DistilGPT2), and the top-5 head sets are disjoint.",
        "proposed_claim": "Zeroing a head-sized slice after the attention output projection does not ablate a single head and selects different heads than pre-projection ablation.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r1",
          "r2",
          "r3",
